---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../../components/PageHero.astro";
import { blogPosts } from "../../../data/blogPosts";

const post = blogPosts.find((p) => p.slug === "how-much-do-thumbnail-artists-get-paid")!;

const tiers = [
  { level: "Beginner / budget", rate: "$5 – $30", fit: "Simple template work, low volume, getting started" },
  { level: "Mid-level", rate: "$30 – $50", fit: "Custom compositing, clean cut-outs, a good eye for layout" },
  { level: "Premium specialist", rate: "$100 – $300+", fit: "Established channels, designers who study analytics and test variants" },
];

const microFaqs = [
  {
    q: "How much does a YouTube thumbnail cost?",
    a: "For most small and mid-sized channels, between about $5 and $50 per thumbnail. Premium designers who work closely with a channel's data commonly charge $100 to $300 or more, and a handful of top creators pay far above that.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much does MrBeast pay for a thumbnail?",
    a: "MrBeast has said he pays around $10,000 per thumbnail, a figure widely reported in the press. It's a self-reported number for one of YouTube's largest channels, so don't treat it as a typical market rate.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is thumbnail design a good side job?",
    a: "It can be. Experienced designers can finish a thumbnail quickly, and recurring clients on retainers make income more predictable. Rates and demand vary a lot, though, and AI image tools are putting pressure on the low end of the market, so building a distinct style and a results-focused portfolio matters.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I pay per thumbnail or on a monthly retainer?",
    a: "Per-thumbnail pricing is simple for occasional uploads. If you publish several videos a week, a package or monthly retainer is usually cheaper per image and gives the designer time to learn your channel's style.",
  },
  {
    q: "How can I tell if a thumbnail is worth what I paid?",
    a: "Check it at phone size, run it through a thumbnail analyzer for contrast and readability, and compare click-through rate against your earlier videos once it's live. YouTube Studio's thumbnail testing can compare variants on a real video.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    headline: post.title,
    description: post.description,
    datePublished: post.publishDate,
    dateModified: post.publishDate,
    author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "VT Analyzer" },
    publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "VT Analyzer" },
    mainEntityOfPage: `https://vtanalyzer.site/blog/${post.slug}/`,
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: microFaqs.map((f) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];
---

<Layout title={post.seoTitle} description={post.description} path={`/blog/${post.slug}/`} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article>
    <PageHero eyebrow="Blog" eyebrowHref="/blog/" title={post.title} art={post.cover} artWidth={640} artHeight={360} artFrame>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-mist/60">
        <time datetime={post.publishDate}>
          {new Date(post.publishDate).toLocaleDateString("en-US", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" })}
        </time>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> &middot; </span>
        {post.readTime}
      </p>
    </PageHero>

    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 px-5 py-16 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70 dark:text-smoke sm:text-base">
      <p>
        Whether you're hiring a designer or thinking about becoming one, the first question is the
        same: what does a thumbnail actually cost? There's no official rate card, and the range is
        enormous. This guide lays out the commonly cited ranges, what pushes a price up or down, and
        how the reported MrBeast figure fits in. Treat every number here as a market estimate, not a
        guarantee.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">How Much Do Thumbnail Artists Get Paid?</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Most freelance thumbnail artists charge somewhere between $5 and $50 per thumbnail, with
          premium specialists commanding $100 to $300 or more. Hourly rates quoted for the US tend to
          land around the low-to-mid $20s, though designers who work fast on packages can earn more
          per hour than that suggests.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-sm border border-line dark:border-seam">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-paper-dim dark:bg-night-dim">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-display font-semibold text-ink dark:text-fog">Level</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-display font-semibold text-ink dark:text-fog">Typical price</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-2.5 font-display font-semibold text-ink dark:text-fog">Best for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-ink/10 dark:divide-seam">
              {tiers.map((t) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="px-4 py-2.5">{t.level}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono-num text-xs">{t.rate}</td>
                  <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink/60 dark:text-smoke">{t.fit}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-ink/50 dark:text-smoke">
          Ranges are compiled from commonly cited freelance marketplace and hiring-guide figures and vary by region and year.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">What Changes the Price</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5">
          <li><strong class="text-ink dark:text-fog">Complexity.</strong> A text-over-photo layout is cheaper than a composited scene with multiple cut-outs and custom effects, such as a detailed Fortnite thumbnail with a rebuilt thumbnail background.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink dark:text-fog">Volume.</strong> Packages and retainers usually bring the per-image price down.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink dark:text-fog">Turnaround.</strong> Rush work costs more.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink dark:text-fog">Strategy.</strong> Designers who help choose the concept, test variants, and review performance charge more than those who only execute a brief.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink dark:text-fog">Experience and results.</strong> A portfolio that links designs to better click-through rates justifies a higher rate.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">How Much Does MrBeast Pay for a Thumbnail?</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          MrBeast has said that a thumbnail is worth around $10,000 to him, and outlets such as
          Rest of World and Social Media Today have repeated the figure. Reporting also describes his
          team testing up to 20 variations per video and brainstorming dozens of thumbnail and title
          concepts before picking one. That's a self-reported number from one of the largest channels on
          the platform, and it reflects iteration, testing, and the value of a single video's reach rather
          than a normal freelance price. If you want to learn from that process without the budget, read
          our FAQ on
          <a href="/faq/#how-do-i-create-a-mrbeast-thumbnail" class="text-red-dark dark:text-red underline underline-offset-2">how to create a MrBeast thumbnail</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">If You're a Creator Hiring a Designer</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Send a clear brief with the video title, the one idea the thumbnail must communicate, and
          reference thumbnails you like. If you study references, you can save any public YT thumbnail
          by its direct link, no thumbnail downloader needed, as we explain in our
          <a href="/blog/how-to-download-a-youtube-thumbnail/" class="text-red-dark dark:text-red underline underline-offset-2">download guide</a>.
          Ask for the file at the standard YouTube thumbnail size of 1280×720, then check the result at
          phone size and in our <a href="/" class="text-red-dark dark:text-red underline underline-offset-2">free thumbnail analyzer</a>
          before you publish.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">If You Want to Become a Thumbnail Artist</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Start with a small portfolio built around one niche, such as gaming, since specialists are
          easier to hire than generalists. Learn what a thumbnail is trying to do, practice the layout
          habits in our
          <a href="/blog/how-to-make-a-youtube-thumbnail/" class="text-red-dark dark:text-red underline underline-offset-2">guide to making a YouTube thumbnail</a>,
          and quote clients per thumbnail at first, then move to packages once you have repeat work. Price
          to cover your time, since the going rate for beginners is low and AI tools keep pushing
          generic work toward the bottom of the market.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-fog">Common Questions About Thumbnail Pay</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 divide-y divide-ink/10 dark:divide-seam">
          {microFaqs.map((f) => (
            <div class="py-5 first:pt-0">
              <h3 class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-ink dark:text-fog">{f.q}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2">{f.a}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
